  "id": "v37-flow-object-serial",
  "asserts": "`flow --object` over an identity that is EXACT. A `sensorium-ts` capture of an object carries a serial minted once from a WeakMap and never reused, so two sightings of one serial are one object -- not a hedge, and not CPython's memory address, which is recycled and which every line of the existing caveat and gap analysis exists to qualify. On this basis the header says the serial is never reused, the footer reads `continuity: exact (serial identity)`, and NONE of `unwitnessed`, `spanned by`, `ADDRESS REUSED` or `NEW OBJECT` may print: they are corroboration for a continuity this recording does not have to corroborate. What the two sightings DO show is the mutation -- one object, two renderings. The gate moves with the basis (ruling R13): `--object` needs `object_identity` and not `line`, because a serial rides on every capture; `--value` still needs `line`.",
